{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4789-abcd-maw-foundation-01",
    "name": "MAW Foundation — Sample Server",
    "description": "Dynamic RBAC sample-server (`createDynamicExpressAuth` + module registry).\n\n**Setup**\n1. `npm run sample:server`\n2. Import this collection + `local.postman_environment.json`\n3. Select **MAW Foundation — Local**\n4. Run **Login as Owner** (or Manager / Clerk) — tests persist `accessToken` / `refreshToken` on the **collection**\n\nProtected routes send `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}`.\n\nPermission codes are `Action_Module` (e.g. `Read_Reports`). Owner is a superuser and bypasses checks. Manager/clerk use the seeded role map.\n\n**Seeded users** (password `password123`)\n| Email | Role | Audience | `/reports` | `/orders` | `/inventory` | `GET /billing` | `POST /billing` | `GET /audit-logs` | `GET /audit-logs/export` | `/admin/users` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| owner@demo.test | owner | admin | 200 | 200 | 200 | 200 | 200 | 200 | 200 | 200 |\n| manager@demo.test | manager | admin | 200 | 200 | 200 | 403 (no `Read_Billing`) | 200 | 200 | 403 (no `Export_AuditLogs`) | 403 (no `Read_Users`) |\n| clerk@demo.test | clerk | operator | 403 | 200 | 403 | 403 (no `Read_Billing`) | 200 | 403 (wrong audience) | 403 (wrong audience) | 403 (wrong audience) |",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "sessionRole", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl')) {",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('baseUrl', 'http://localhost:4000');",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Health & catalog",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET Health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('server is up', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().ok).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Liveness check. No auth."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET Modules",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns registered modules', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.modules).to.be.an('array').and.not.empty;",
                  "  const keys = body.modules.map((m) => m.key);",
                  "  pm.expect(keys).to.include.members(['users', 'reports', 'orders', 'inventory', 'billing', 'audit-logs']);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/modules",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["modules"]
            },
            "description": "Module registry dump (no auth): key, name, audience, permission codes, feature code. This is the catalog the sync engine upserts on boot."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 Catalog",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "body": "{\n  \"modules\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"users\",\n      \"name\": \"Users\",\n      \"audience\": \"admin\",\n      \"permissions\": [\"Read_Users\", \"Create_Users\", \"Update_Users\", \"Delete_Users\"],\n      \"feature\": \"users\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"reports\",\n      \"name\": \"Reports\",\n      \"audience\": \"admin\",\n      \"permissions\": [\"Read_Reports\", \"Create_Reports\"],\n      \"feature\": \"reports\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Authentication",
      "description": "Login / logout, JWT access token, rotating refresh token. Login also returns `permissions` (`Action_Module`) and `modules` for the UI.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST Login as Owner",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('login succeeded', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.tokens.refreshToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionRole', body.session.role);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', body.session.userId);",
                  "  pm.test('session + token pair + catalog', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.session.role).to.eql('owner');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.session.audience).to.eql('admin');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.tokens.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(body.tokens.refreshToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(body.permissions).to.be.an('array');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.modules).to.be.an('array').and.not.empty;",
                  "  });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"owner@demo.test\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Owner is a superuser (`superuserRoles: ['owner']`) and maps to the admin role, so permission checks are bypassed. `permissions` is empty because admin does not need an explicit grant list."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "body": "{\n  \"session\": {\n    \"userId\": \"u-owner\",\n    \"tenantId\": \"demo-tenant\",\n    \"role\": \"owner\",\n    \"audience\": \"admin\",\n    \"entitlements\": [\"users\", \"reports\", \"orders\", \"inventory\", \"billing\"],\n    \"capabilities\": [],\n    \"rolePermissions\": {}\n  },\n  \"tokens\": {\n    \"accessToken\": \"eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...\",\n    \"refreshToken\": \"<hex>\"\n  },\n  \"permissions\": [],\n  \"modules\": [{ \"key\": \"users\", \"name\": \"Users\", \"audience\": \"admin\" }]\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST Login as Manager",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('login succeeded', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.tokens.refreshToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionRole', body.session.role);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', body.session.userId);",
                  "  pm.test('manager grants', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.session.role).to.eql('manager');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.session.audience).to.eql('admin');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.permissions).to.include.members(['Read_Reports', 'Read_Orders', 'Create_Orders', 'Read_Inventory', 'Create_Billing', 'Read_AuditLogs']);",
                  "    pm.expect(body.permissions).to.not.include('Read_Users');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.permissions).to.not.include('Read_Billing');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.permissions).to.not.include('Export_AuditLogs');",
                  "  });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"manager@demo.test\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Grants: Read_Reports, Create_Reports, Read_Orders, Create_Orders, Update_Orders, Read_Inventory, Create_Billing, Read_AuditLogs. No Read_Users, no Read_Billing, no Export_AuditLogs."
          }
